# Heavy ML stack for the local models (BGE-M3 embedder, bge-reranker-v2-m3; blueprint §3.4, §3.6, §12.9).
# Kept out of requirements.txt so CI and the CPU image stay light. app/core/device.py and app/retrieval/*
# import torch / FlagEmbedding lazily, so the base install works without this file.
#
# GPU (RTX 3050, CUDA): install the CUDA build of torch from the PyTorch index FIRST, then the rest.
# cu128 is the current stable CUDA wheel line; cu126 also works on the 3050 (Ampere, sm_86). Check
# https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/ for the current index before installing.
#
#   UV_LINK_MODE=copy uv pip install --python .venv torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128
#   UV_LINK_MODE=copy uv pip install --python .venv -r requirements-ml.in -c requirements.txt
#
# CPU only (deployment host without a GPU):
#
#   UV_LINK_MODE=copy uv pip install --python .venv torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
#   UV_LINK_MODE=copy uv pip install --python .venv -r requirements-ml.in -c requirements.txt
#
# Pinning: requirements-ml.txt is not committed yet, because resolving torch from the CUDA index pulls
# multi-GB wheels. When the stack is installed on the dev machine, pin it with
#
#   uv pip compile requirements-ml.in -c requirements.txt -o requirements-ml.txt \
#       --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128 --index-strategy unsafe-best-match
#
# Model weights (~2.3 GB BGE-M3 + ~2.3 GB reranker) download from the Hugging Face Hub on first use into
# HF_HOME. Verify the whole stack with:
#   RUN_LIVE_MODELS=1 .venv/Scripts/python -m pytest -m live tests/integration/test_retrieval_live.py

